[[0.16, "Imagine 100 spark executors processing"], [2.34, "data perfectly fine until you"], [4.02, "add one groupBy and"], [5.38, "suddenly your spark job slows"], [6.66, "down but why let's say"], [7.78, "you have billions of orders"], [9.12, "distributed across 100 executors and"], [11.4, "everything is running in parallel"], [12.66, "no problem so far and"], [14.2, "now you run a df.groupBy"], [16.34, "country.count and now things get"], [18.62, "interesting now spark needs data"], [20.46, "for the same country to"], [21.64, "reach the same shuffle partition"], [23.2, "so intermediate data sitting on"], [24.96, "one executor may need to"], [26.76, "move to another and that's"], [28.3, "called shuffle can be very"], [30.0, "expensive operation by the way"], [31.1, "because spark may need to"], [32.64, "serialize the data write it"], [34.32, "to disk adding disk i/o"], [36.22, "overhead transfer it across the"], [38.04, "network adding network i/o cost"], [40.4, "and then this next stage"], [42.42, "fetch the reader reads and"], [44.64, "deserialize it and performs the"], [46.08, "required aggregation all of this"], [47.64, "adds to shuffle overhead and"], [49.6, "while this happens some tasks"], [51.38, "may spend more time waiting"], [53.0, "for the data than actually"], [54.2, "processing it but here is"], [55.5, "what most people miss when"], [57.54, "data movement is the bottleneck"], [59.42, "moving less data can help"], [61.42, "more than adding more executors"], [63.18, "so whenever possible filter unnecessary"], [65.28, "rows and columns before a"], [66.78, "shuffle and avoid unnecessary shuffles"], [69.76, "altogether and speaking of reducing"], [71.9, "data movement that's where a"], [73.44, "powerful optimization called broadcast join"], [75.74, "and let's cover that next"], [77.38, "and this was the episode"], [78.88, "3 of spark performance"]]